# Intent: The setup page stays open for several networks (old firmware, owner 2026-11-17). It used to close three seconds after the first network was saved, so a second network needed a second trip through setup. Now after a save the page clears its network name, password and travel key, says "Saved. Add another network above, or tap Finish when you are done." and shows a Finish button. Finish sends the same setup code in a final request and the unit leaves setup 1.5 s later; otherwise setup ends when its window (8 minutes) ends, as before. Every save still joins the network first and writes only what worked, and the setup code check and the five-wrong-codes lock apply to Finish as well. Two new strings (Finish, Done), English and Spanish; the page stays under its 5 KB budget.
# Placement: unit (the setup page is the unit's own and works with the host off)
# Upstream: firmware/portal/ of this tree (patches P01 to P05), which replaces the access point source of 78/esp-wifi-connect (MIT); the old firmware's page edit
# Check after a flash: add two networks in one visit: after the first the page says Saved with a Finish button and stays usable; after the second, tap Finish: the page says Done and the unit leaves setup and joins; with no Finish the unit leaves setup when the 8 minute window ends. A wrong code on Finish is refused.
# Kconfig: MAIPAI_WIFI_PORTAL.

